The ROS Disc Project (2024)

This project was undertaken by Eric Lin (class of 2024)
and Helios Hu (class of 2025), with Professor Yap
in the Spring of 2024.  Eric and Helios teamed up to
work together and made great progress (Jan-Apr).

We wanted to port the C++ disc program (the first SSS algorithm,
from 2013) to the ROS framework, to give us an online demo that
is accessible by any browser.  The ROS platform was based on Windows
(it seems that the MacOS version of ROS is substandard).
The original C++ disc code is
available from the Core Library https://cs.nyu.edu/exact/.

Their work is found in github:

https://github.com/exl7954/disc-path-gui

We plan to install a server for this 
See the screenshot in this folder of the GUI interface.

--Chee
19 Apr 2024



